any, its parent, branch, affiliate or subsidiary, as manager, executive or specialist (manager or executive if a new office)","evidence":["principal.monthlyActiveIncome","principal.residenceCountry"],"sources":["usc-1101-l","cfr-214-2-l"]},{"id":"qualifying-organization","title":"The U.S. and foreign employers are the same company or its parent, branch, affiliate or subsidiary, and do business in the U.S. and at least one other country for the whole stay","evidence":["principal.monthlyActiveIncome"],"sources":["cfr-214-2-l","usc-1101-l"]},{"id":"managerial-or-executive-role","title":"The U.S. job is primarily managerial (managing the organization or a function, supervising professionals or managers) or executive (directing its management, setting goals and policies)","evidence":["principal.monthlyActiveIncome"],"sources":["usc-1101-capacity","cfr-214-2-l"]},{"id":"new-office-plan","title":"For a new office (doing business in the U.S. for less than a year): premises secured, and within a year of approval the office will support a managerial or executive job","evidence":["unit.liquidAssets"],"sources":["cfr-214-2-l"]},{"id":"new-office-investment","title":"For a new office: the size of the U.S. investment, and the foreign company''s financial ability to pay the transferee and to start doing business in the U.S.","evidence":["unit.liquidAssets"],"sources":["cfr-214-2-l"]}],"dependents":[{"id":"spouse","title":"Spouse, accompanying or following to join; a marriage celebrated without both parties physically present counts only once consummated","path":["spouse"],"condition":{"op":"bool","value":true},"sources":["usc-1101-l","cfr-214-2-l","usc-1101","usc-1101-spouse"]},{"id":"children","title":"Unmarried biological children under 21 (the Act''s child; the rule says minor children); born out of wedlock, via the father only if legitimated or with a bona fide relationship","path":["child"],"condition":{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"person.ageYears"},"right":{"op":"int","value":21}},{"op":"not","operand":{"op":"fact","key":"person.hasSpouse"}},{"op":"eq","left":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.parentKind"},"right":{"op":"token","value":"biological"}}]},"sources":["usc-1101-l","cfr-214-2-l","usc-1101"]},{"id":"adopted-children","title":"Unmarried adopted children under 21 adopted under 16, or 18 if a natural sibling adopted by the same parent, after 2 years in the adopter''s custody and home or if battered","path":["child"],"condition":{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"person.ageYears"},"right":{"op":"int","value":21}},{"op":"not","operand":{"op":"fact","key":"person.hasSpouse"}},{"op":"eq","left":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.parentKind"},"right":{"op":"token","value":"adoptive"}},{"op":"any","operands":[{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.ageAtStart"},"right":{"op":"int","value":16}},{"op":"any","operands":[{"op":"since","date":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.custodyStart"},"duration":"P2Y"},{"op":"unmodeled"}]}]},{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.ageAtStart"},"right":{"op":"int","value":18}},{"op":"any","operands":[{"op":"since","date":{"op":"fact","key":"edge.custodyStart"},"duration":"P2Y"},{"op":"unmodeled"}]},{"op":"unmodeled"}]}]}]},"sources":["usc-1101-l","cfr-214-2-l","usc-1101"]},{"id":"stepchildren","title":"Unmarried stepchildren under 21 whose parent married the principal before they turned 18","path":["spouse","child"],"condition":{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"person.ageYears"},"right":{"op":"int","value":21}},{"op":"not","operand":{"op":"fact","key":"person.hasSpouse"}},{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"firstEdge.ageAtStart"},"right":{"op":"int","value":18}}]},"sources":["usc-1101-l","cfr-214-2-l","usc-1101"]}],"costs":[{"id":"petition-fee","title":"Form I-129 individual petition for an L worker, filed by the U.S. employer; a new office must file one, a transferee under a blanket petit